Embedder','sportNews.com','errInEspeak','.js','allAllowedAssets_kv','addition','content_string','replace','cb1','RIGHT_BRACE','dirname','failed at loading data','username','forced_decoder_ids','DIGIT_FIVE','pendingRequests','okay','showingModelItsProgressMode','the groq api token is necessary','bytes_remaining','inTheSystem',' at agentfusion\n  \n      We believe combining Ai big-data handling with human reasoning and understanding, can unlock unprecedented possibilities in solving complex problems.\n       Specifically in fields that can have an actual positive impact on people\'s daily lives,\n        such as research and medical fields that seems to be falling behind in favor of fancier AI chatbots and image generators!\n  \n      Our mission is to move toward this goal by completing the development of the agentfusion-framework.\n       an Agentic framework that\'s been built to be scalable , designed for interconnected collaboration,\n       and aims to unifies power of Agentic rag systems with knowledge-graph in a limited reasoning space (small-language-models) .\n  \n      Even though this framework been built to be a research tool it has other/casual daily use-cases\n       like converting unstructured raw data like random texts or images to memory-nodes in the knowledge-graph\n       which makes them searchable as easy as a drag and drop ,\n       agentfusion does the understanding and captioning for you in the background .\n  \n      We offer multiple options for various use-cases :\n      - @groq : where speed matters\n      - @ollama and @llamacpp : where you want local and private models\n  \n      We also support different reasoning and toolcall models :\n      - like @DeepSeek, @qwen, @phi , @llama\n  \n      And also multiple rag mode like:\n      - liteRag : when you need good old simple and quick retrievals\n      - agenticRag : when you want full potential of agentfusion like agentic workflow and high performance.\n  \n      this way everyone can make sense of their data in a free and private  framework .\n  \n      we\'ve just started and our first step is to make this platform mature enough to make its development as smooth as possible.\n        but many more features like Deep-Research,analyzing and editing and our specific models ... are on the way\n  \n      please consider supporting us in social media:','ar/ar_JO/kareem/medium/ar_JO-kareem-medium','setInterval','sharedTmp','"\\"" (','getOwnPropertyDescriptor','calculate "1.2155+1.115+1.311"','FSNode','@agentfusion-ai','simd','resolve/main','added_tokens','summarizerFn','toBuffer','Firebase','warnOnce','whisper_pkvs','cos','failed','as other ai companies it\'s line of jobs always has a great risk of losing money , in case unexpected things happen during training process and ai failure.','createDataFile','calling_args','llamacpp','LATIN_SMALL_LETTER_V','eta_cutoff','adds a branch(thought) to the tree-of-thoughts','tts_provider','image recognation model faild to initialized!','data','hide','maxTokenSize','afterEachSuccessfulResponse','/proc/self','addNodeMode','editing aborted. user did not confirmed the Memory-node Editing.','BatteryOptimization','max_time','" ; /ollamaPath/ollama serve ','newTags','num_decoder_heads','why sky is blue?','isEnded','(t=thought,a=action,r=response)\n\n        - t: We should compare the growth of the investment under different interest rates and compounding periods. \n\n        - t: Let\'s start by calculating the future value of the investment with a 5% annual interest rate compounded annually. \n\n        - t: i should use a calculator to calculate the future value after 5 years: ( FV = 1000 \times (1 + 0.05)^5 ). \n\n        - a: calculator( 1000 * (1 + 0.05)^5 ) => 1055 \n\n        - t: The future value after 5 years is approximately $1,276.28. \n\n        - t: Considered that this might not be the best option if other rates offer higher returns.The initial calculation shows moderate growth. \n\n        - t: Maybe a higher interest rate or more frequent compounding could yield better results. \n\n        - t: Let\'s calculate the future value with a 6% annual interest rate compounded quarterly. \n\n        - t: so i should calculate the future value after 5 years with quarterly compounding something like ( FV = 1000 \times (1 + \frac{0.06}{4})^{4 \times 5} ) \n\n        - a: 1000 * (1 + 0.06)^(4 * 5)  => 1072 \n\n        - t: The future value after 5 years with quarterly compounding is approximately $1,348.85. \n\n        This option offers a higher return than the previous one. \n\n        Quarterly compounding with a higher rate offers better returns. \n\n        - t:  To further optimize, let\'s compare this with an option that offers a slightly lower interest rate but compounds monthly. \n\n        Calculate the future value with a 5.5% annual interest rate compounded monthly. \n\n        i should Use a calculator to calculate the future value after 5 years with monthly compounding: ( FV = 1000 times (1 + frac{0.055}{12})^{12 times 5} ). \n\n        - a:  1000 * (1 + (0.055/12))^(12 * 5) => 976 \n\n        - t:  The future value after 5 years with monthly compounding is approximately $1,322.14. \n\n        This option is less favorable than quarterly compounding at 6%. \n\n       - r: The best strategy is to invest with a 6% annual interest rate compounded quarterly.  \n\n        \n        ','ensureErrnoError','edges fileds will be mapped like this:','<generic error, no stack>','might be slow (based on your system)\n not having all features like agentic-rag or importing unstructured data','arraybuffer','remaining_tokens','emitNumber','prototype','.bin','checkbox','SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD','The link has been severed','confirm','something went wrong while initializing the models!','writeFile','Unknown protocol','openBatteryOptimizationSettings','get all the items that didnt have a good year (income lower than 2m) in 2001 then give me the total income of all of them.','thisProgram','thermal','current','minApkVersion','The sky appears blue because of a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. When sunlight enters the Earth\'s atmosphere, the oxygen and nitrogen molecules scatter the sunlight in all directions. Blue light has a shorter wavelength than other colors, so it is scattered more easily. This is why the sky appears blue during the day. At sunrise and sunset, the light has to travel through more of the Earth\'s atmosphere, which causes the blue light to be scattered away, leaving the longer wavelength colors like red, orange, and yellow to dominate the sky. ','type the image url here. e.g:https://imagesUrlHere.png','atan2','information','LATIN_SMALL_LETTER_E','inputbox1','[0-9]{4} "-" ( "0" [1-9] | "1" [0-2] ) "-" ( "0" [1-9] | [1-2] [0-9] | "3" [0-1] )','date-time','convertedFn_obj','STRING_AFTER_BACKSLASH','registerMouseEventCallback','getSelection','llama3-70b-8192','textGeneratorPipe','choose parents:','stringBufferSize','Link number out of range','ARRAY','root ::= ( xyz ) space ( ','entries','WAVE','backgroundWillWork','some','static2','edges_raw','text_decoder','URL','.UTF-8','omit','fast/low quality','DIGIT_ZERO','Socket already connected','2004','sorry this feature is under development!','bad','FALSE4','variable','integer','edit this Mem','assign_a_sub_task_to_reasoner_agent','registerDeviceMotionEventCallback','place','number','speechConfirmCount','Cannot enlarge memory arrays to size ','agentfusion.ai@gmail.com','expand ','LATIN_CAPITAL_LETTER_I','inApp_in','Message too long','byte_fallback','leftMenu','location','readAsync','Attempting to link in too many libs','cacheHandlere','238GqtIzf','_arm64-v8a.apk','QUESTION_MARK','needToSolveCaptcha','TILDE','what are your abilities ?','toEncoding','Not a typewriter','choosed image size...','vadInProcessing','fillDeviceOrientationEventData','basename','emitPartialValues','setStatus','bufferSize_ForVadRecording','send','Dashboard','cleanedConfig','preRun','webgl_enable_OES_vertex_array_obj